ime video calling and live  streaming so when you have that  background blur effect turned on during  face time it's going to make it easier  and more accurate now I know the entire  iPad lineup has transitioned to using  the 12 megapixel Ultra wide camera with  Center Stage support where it basically  follows you around wherever you go now  some people were thinking that Apple  would put that ultrawide camera onto the  iPhones but based on the numbers and the  aperture that I'm seeing here I do not  think that is the case first of all if  you look at the iPad Pro with the ultra  wide camera it has an F 2.4 aperture and  that's because when you go Ultra wide it  it's harder to have a faster f-stop or  taking in more light it's harder to make  that happen without making the lens  massive so because of this the fact that  apple is going reverse and letting in  more light with an F 1.9 aperture kind  of shows that it's going to be another  12 megapixel camera that's just going to  be better with better lenses I mean  hopefully it might be like a 16  megapixel that would really be awesome  or maybe even more but I don't think it  is going to be ultra wide now moving on  we finally got our first iPhone 14 molds  as you can see here is our lineup we now  finally have two iPhone 14 Max models we  have the regular one as you can see  right here it has just the Dual lenses  then you have the pro Max one thing I  can tell is that the actual camera  lenses themselves are wider they're just  bulkier compared to the ones on the  regular models look at how massive this  camera bump is compared to the size of  this 6.1 inch iPhone it is huge and if  you are wondering why it is that big  let's get right into it over a full year  ago Ming Shaco came out and said that  the 2022 iPhones will feature a main 48  megapixel camera that can shoot 8K video  so that is why the camera bumps are  going to be just so massive this year  because we're getting the biggest camera  update and change that we have ever seen  on the iPhone ever now moving on we  actually got a weibo leak talking about  the main Sony sensor that's going to be  going into the iPhone 14 Pro Models  first of all they gave us info on the  sensor size which is absolutely massive  one by 1.3 millimeter so it's going to  be huge and it confirms that they are  going to be able to record 8K video at  60 FPS at least the sensor is capable of  doing this now with that said those were  the leaks for the iPhone 14 lineup and I  personally think that they are going to  be huge however  the leaks that we thought we were gonna  get this year in terms of the brand new  redesign with the glass on both sides as  you can see in this render that I had  renders by Shailesh create for me you  have glass on both sides and you have  the protruding camera bumps right there  along with a circular volume buttons  which were actually leaked from Front  Page Tech and according to this video he  made he basically admitted that the real  iPhone 14 is not gonna have a flat glass  back he basically said that sometimes he  gets his leaks early so he believes that  the leaks that he got in terms of the  glass on both sides with the flush back  design and the single camera cutouts he  thinks those are actually destined for  next year's iPhone 15 instead now with  that said I did make a video on how the  iPhone 14 pro could have USBC and that  was based around the fact that it was  going to be getting this full redesign  with the titanium chassis it looks like  we are not going to be potentially  getting USBC until next year or apple  might go all out remove the ports  completely and go fully Wireless that  might be one reason why you might skip  out on the iPhone 14 lineup this year  and just wait another year with your  current phone and just look at this this  is a darker model you can see the glass  on both sides you see these new speaker  grilles which are based on John  Prosser's leaks and you have USB type c  w